            "feedback": {
              "content_id": "default_outcome_12",
              "html": ""
            },
            "labelled_as_correct": false
          },
          "hints": [],
          "solution": null
        }
      },
      "Comparison Practice": {
        "content": {
          "content_id": "content_0",
          "html": "<p>Omar was at the sports club and saw Coach Kim.</p><p>\u201cGood morning Coach Kim,\u201d Omar said.</p><p>\u201cHi Omar!\u201d Coach Kim replied.</p><p>Omar looked at the leaderboard with each club member\u2019s long jump measurements on it. \u201cI want to know how to convert units, so that the leaderboard measurements are all in the same units.\u201d he said.</p><p>\u201cLet\u2019s start by reviewing how to compare measurements that are in the same unit,\u201d Coach Kim replied. \u201cWhich of these would be the longest long jump?\u201d</p>"
        },
        "interaction": {
          "id": "MultipleChoiceInput",
          "customization_args": {
            "choices": {
              "value": [
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_3",
                  "html": "<p>400 cm</p>"
                },
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_4",
                  "html": "<p>390 cm</p>"
                },
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_5",
                  "html": "<p>396 cm</p>"
                },
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_6",
                  "html": "<p>381 cm</p>"
                }
              ]
            },
            "showChoicesInShuffledOrder": {
              "value": true
            }
          },
          "answer_groups": [
            {
              "rule_specs": [
                {
                  "rule_type": "Equals",
                  "inputs": {
                    "x": 0
                  }
                }
              ],
              "outcome": {
                "dest": "Unit Conversion Intro",
                "feedback": {
                  "content_id": "feedback_2",
                  "html": "<p>Correct!</p>"
                },
                "labelled_as_correct": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "default_outcome": {
            "dest": "Comparison Practice",
            "feedback": {
              "content_id": "default_outcome_1",
              "html": "<p>No, that's not correct.</p>"
            },
            "labelled_as_correct": false
          },
          "hints": [],
          "solution": null
        }
      },
      "Unit Conversion Intro": {
        "content": {
          "content_id": "content_36",
          "html": "<p>\u201cThat was easy,\u201d Omar said. He pointed at the leaderboard. \u201cBut the actual long jump measurements are in different units, like meters and centimeters.\u201d</p><p>\u201cLet\u2019s learn how to convert all these measurements to the same unit so you can compare easily,\u201d Coach Kim replied. \u201cIn the metric system, to convert a measurement from one unit to another, you first need to know the relationship between the two units.\u201d</p><p>\u201cWhat is a metric system? And what is the relationship between two units?\u201d Omar asked.</p><p>She continued. \u201cThe metric system is a pattern of measurement based on a decimal system. Many countries decided to follow the same standard for the metric system so it is easier to communicate! It is called the International System of Units (SI). As for relationships between two units, they simply tell us how much of one unit is in another, one example would be that there are 1000 meters in 1 kilometer. That is because \u201ckilo\u201d means 1000, like so.\u201d</p><p>\u201cThese units are part of the metric system, which is a pattern of measurement based on a decimal system and it is used in many countries to make it easier to communicate! We put prefixes before the meter to shift between different units.\u201d</p><p>\u201cNow, if \u201ccenti\u201d means one hundredth (1/100), what is the mathematical relationship between meters and centimeters?\u201d</p>"
        },
        "interaction": {
          "id": "MultipleChoiceInput",
          "customization_args": {
            "choices": {
              "value": [
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_39",
                  "html": "<p>100 cm = 100 m</p>"
                },
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_40",
                  "html": "<p>100 cm = 1 cm</p>"
                },
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_41",
                  "html": "<p>100 m = 1 cm</p>"
                },
                {
                  "content_id": "ca_choices_42",
                  "html": "<p>1 m = 100 cm</p>"
                }
              ]
            },
            "showChoicesInShuffledOrder": {
              "value": true
            }
          },
          "answer_groups": [
            {
              "rule_specs": [
                {
                  "rule_type": "Equals",
                  "inputs": {
                    "x": 3
                  }
                }
              ],
              "outcome": {
                "dest": "Unit Conversion 2",
                "feedback": {
                  "content_id": "feedback_38",
                  "html": "<p>Correct!</p>"
                },
                "labelled_as_correct": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "default_outcome": {
            "dest": "Unit Conversion Intro",
            "feedback": {
