      "Unit conversion 3": {
        "content": {
          "content_id": "content_46",
          "html": "<p>\u201cGreat, we know now that: there are 1000 meters in one kilometer and that there are 100 centimeters in one meter.\u201d Coach Kim said.</p><p>\u201cOkay, but how can we use that to convert units,\u201d asked Omar.</p><p>\u201cRight,\u201d Coach Kim said. \u201cHere is an example:\u201d</p><p>2000 meters is the same as 2 kilometers because we know that 1000 m = 1 km!&nbsp;</p><p>\u201cI see, since I know that 1000 m = 1 km, if I have 5km I know it is the same as 5000m, right?\u201d Omar said. \u201cSo, knowing that 100 cm = 1 m, what is 3 m in centimeters?\u201d</p>"
        },
        "interaction": {
          "id": "NumberWithUnits",
          "customization_args": {},
          "answer_groups": [
            {
              "rule_specs": [
                {
                  "rule_type": "IsEqualTo",
